    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** pacing the roster at an elite 83.29 score. His matchup against Rea is the primary driver, bolstered by a significant 16% park factor advantage and an expected SP skill boost of 17%. While we concede a minor 2% efficiency hit due to his status as an elite SB threat facing a pitcher with a favorable hold rate, his combination of power and order placement at #1 makes him the clear anchor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (77.19) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) offer high-floor production against favorable SP_xERA marks above 5.00. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a high-value play today; despite his lower base, the 14% platoon edge and the favorable matchup against Arrighetti elevate him to a 74.55 rating, making him a cornerstone for our middle infield output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Miguel Vargas**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 53.40 rating. While his xwOBA of .406 is elite and his speed metrics against Bennett are favorable, he lacked the volume of surrounding lineup protection found in our starters. The optimizer ultimately favored the balanced production of **Jacob Wilson** and **Curtis Mead**, who benefit more substantially from their respective park and SP skill matchups. Note that we face some risk with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for our outfielders; should **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, or **Cole Carrigg** drop significantly in their respective batting orders, their daily efficiency scores will be subject to recalibration. Finally, exercise caution with **Heliot Ramos**; despite his leadoff spot, he faces the formidable Cease (2.97 xERA), and his low 46.17 score reflects the reality that he is currently acting as a cap-preservation play rather than a primary contributor today.",
